WARNING: Optimizing structures in the presence of point charges using internal coordinates
Since the internal coordinates do not consider the translational and rotational degrees of freedom,
the molecule will NOT translate or rotate in the point charge's field!
If this is not the desired behavior, please do the geometry optimization under Cartesian
coordinates instead, by specifying !COpt or %geom coordsys cartesian end.


WARNING: Geometry Optimization
  ===> : Switching off AutoStart
         For restart on a previous wavefunction, please use MOREAD

WARNING: The chosen methods will break translational/rotational symmetry
  ===> : Will NOT project out the translational and rotational degrees of freedom
         of the Hessians, in case Hessians are calculated!

WARNING: The chosen methods will break translational symmetry
  ===> : Will NOT exploit translational invariance of the Hessians,
         in case Hessians are calculated!

WARNING: The chosen methods will break translational symmetry
  ===> : Will NOT make the numerical gradients translationally invariant,
         in case numerical gradients are calculated!

